  "coverage_rules": [
    "Every leaf below is required target coverage; parent IDs are grouping references and never close a leaf.",
    "Leaf labels address the corresponding prose requirement; they do not relax any qualifier in the parent model/operation contract.",
    "The library-wide coverage disposition must cover every required ID, with no omissions or unknown IDs. A support entry may cover several IDs sharing its exact profiles, ownership and evidence; repeated metadata is unnecessary. Duplicate ID/profile claims are consolidated rather than counted twice.",
    "A well-formed manifest may report incomplete implementation. Comprehensive completion additionally requires supported coverage for every target minimum and required interaction through lawful profiles.",
    "Inapplicable is a per-profile judgement requiring semantic reason; it cannot remove a required target leaf from library-wide completion.",
    "Alternative implementations retain separate profile-qualified claims. Completion aggregates only qualified applicable evidence, never unsupported/inapplicable labels.",
    "Accountable owner is a stable team/role with authority over contract and evidence; ownership transfer is versioned, preserving historical attribution.",
    "A supported entry has immutable evidence revisions and no remaining required work within its conformance scope.",
    "Missing implementation/profile/owner bindings are explicit unassigned values only on unimplemented entries; they cannot appear on entries of any other status (the schema's conditional rules reject them for supported, unsupported-by-this-implementation and inapplicable entries).",
    "Cross-cutting applicability is checked on every realised capability, not discharged once by one example.",
    "Coverage keys are not atom, module, package, team or test boundaries. One meaningful proof/journey can establish several requirements; unrelated obligations cannot hide behind a parent status.",
    "Support entries are immutable by (entry_id, entry_revision). First revision is 1 with null predecessor_ref; each update appends the next revision with predecessor_ref equal to entry_id@previous_revision. Conflicting bytes for an existing identity/revision are rejected.",
    "Ownership transfer appends an entry revision with the new accountable_owner; retain the immutable predecessor and its qualification evidence/owner attribution. Carried evidence keeps its original qualification provenance through the predecessor chain; new qualification is new evidence. Schema shape checking alone cannot establish persistence/history integrity.",
    "Implementation sourcing and survey-to-design provenance follow algorithms-and-data-structures-governance-2026-09-08.md. Reference agreement or historical package evidence alone does not qualify an owned implementation; evidence distinguishes independent contract reasoning from source-dependent checks. This policy adds no target leaves and removes none."
  ],
